sxml check - Check that XML documents are namespace-well-formed

Usage: sxml check [--format=FORMAT] FILE...

Checks every FILE against XML 1.0 (Fifth Edition) and Namespaces in
XML 1.0, without building it. Encodings: UTF-8, UTF-16, ISO-8859-1
and US-ASCII. The external DTD subset and external entities are not
read. Each problem is reported on standard error as
FILE:LINE:COLUMN: message; with --format=json, one JSON object on
standard output lists every file with its "status". Exits 1 when a
file is not well-formed, 3 when a file cannot be read.

Options:
  -h, --help           Show this help and exit
      --format=FORMAT  Report format (one of: text, json; default: text)

Arguments:
  FILE  XML document to check; - reads standard input

Examples:
  sxml check document.xml
  sxml check --format=json a.xml b.xml
